Falsifies `file_allocation_table::long_name::verification::every_alias_is_a_legal_short_name`.

The defect: the alias keeps seven base units instead of six, so a long base pushes the `~1` tail to
bytes 7 and 8 and its `1` into the extension. The bytes are all legal short-name bytes, which is
why the harness checks where the tail sits and not only what the bytes are.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(tilde >= 1 && tilde <= 6)`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs
index 0bc37e010..74cab65f6 100644
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ impl LongName {
             None => (units, &[][..]),
         };
         let mut out = [b' '; 11];
-        let base_len = fold(base, &mut out[..6]);
+        let base_len = fold(base, &mut out[..7]);
         if base_len == 0 {
             return None;
         }
